data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","sequence_number":835,"item_id":"msg_0102816b60dcee68016b09a4f971c087d199ba20811918cb5a","output_index":1,"content_index":0,"text":"{\"queries\":[],\"result_json\":\"{\\\"reviews\\\":[{\\\"actor\\\":\\\"sol\\\",\\\"decision\\\":\\\"develop\\\",\\\"ability\\\":null,\\\"reason\\\":\\\"The retrieved eat capability (eat, foundation-forest@1, handler forest.eat) accepts resource targets but does not specify deterministic multi-stack resolution; the reported ambiguity shows the missing behavior. Related capability searches found no demonstrated executable equivalent. Develop only a deterministic owned-stack selector that delegates consumption to existing eating code, not a replacement nutrition or food-safety system.\\\",\\\"specification\\\":\\\"General operation: consume-owned-food, parameterized by explicit resource id and positive integer quantity, available for any applicable actor to study. Accept resource:ID using the existing resource identifier format. At each new execution, consider only actual currently owned, accessible matching stacks that independently contain the requested quantity and satisfy ordinary eat targeting prerequisites. Sort these eligible stacks by harvestedAt ascending, then by exact item id in ascending code-unit order; missing harvest timestamps sort after known timestamps. Select one stack only. Do not combine stacks, substitute resources, gather food or infer safety. If no single eligible stack exists, return an explicit no-single-stack-with-requested-quantity failure; distinguish this from no matching owned stock without exposing other actors' stock. This minimal version deliberately does not aggregate quantities across stacks. Record the resolved exact item id and delegate to eat@foundation-forest@1 / forest.eat with that id and quantity. Record this code dependency and reuse explicitly. Preserve existing eat validation, food condition, nutrition, toxicity, satiety limits and failure behavior; berry nutrition 8 and toxicity 0 are supplied personal knowledge, not defaults for roots, hazelnuts or arbitrary resources. Execution costs exactly the delegated action: one simulation round, 1 energy and the actually consumed quantity of the selected food; selector overhead has no separate material, energy or time cost. Validate before charging or reserving, and atomically recheck ownership, quantity and accessibility when reserving. Use the existing eating escrow and progress implementation, without double charging: resolved identity persists for that execution; interruption cancels under the existing eat rule; cancellation or death releases surviving unconsumed escrow exactly once, with no restoration of consumed food or spent time/energy. Released food retains its real condition, provenance and harvest timestamp and follows ordinary location/ownership rules. Global pauses retain work and costs without advancing time. Resume cannot silently switch the identity of an in-progress execution; a new execution resolves again. Repeating plans count completed executions, never mere selection attempts. Food removal and actual bodily effects commit together under ordinary eating rules, with no creation, healing or bonus nutrition. No background process, maintenance, new stock or lasting physical product is introduced. Emit observable selection/start, interruption/failure and completed-consumption events containing actor, explicit resource, requested quantity, resolved item when applicable, consumed quantity and actual outcome; private inventory candidates remain private. Established selection and execution rules must run in code. Development/review waiting advances no world time.\\\",\\\"learning\\\":1,\\\"experienceReview\\\":\\\"Individual study requires 1 round and 0.2 energy, no materials, through the existing learning process after implementation; it does not grant mastery now or to other actors. Selection, requests, registration, learning and successful resolution alone award no pleasure or satisfaction. Actual completed eating retains existing event-based experience rules and normal nutrition independently of mood; do not create a parallel eating reward, raise caps or modify protected reward accounts, budgets, goals or permissions. Failure provides a factual execution result, not an automatic information-gain award. Physical comfort remains capped at 10.\\\",\\\"visualReview\\\":\\\"Reuse ordinary eating visuals only while actual delegated eating is underway. Provide reusable metadata keyed by operation and event phase, with actor, resource, resolved item when available, quantity, progress and outcome; completion metadata must report actual consumed quantity. Pending selection may show a neutral targeting state, and failure or cancellation must show its true state without an eating-success animation or depleted-stack display. Update stack visuals only from committed inventory changes; show no new food, safety badge or success effect from selection alone.\\\"}]}\"}","logprobs":[]}

